<header><p class="st-kicker">other · Italy</p><h1 class="st-title">Provisional Government of Milan</h1><p class="st-meta">1848 CE – 1848 CE · capital Milan</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The government formed by the Milanese after the Five Days of 1848 drove out the Austrians, which merged Lombardy with Piedmont before Radetzky returned.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>From 18 to 22 March 1848 the people of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/duchy-of-milan">Milan</a> fought the Five Days, barricade battles that forced <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/joseph-radetzky-von-radetz">Marshal Radetzky's</a> Austrian garrison to leave the city. A provisional government headed by the mayor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gabrio-casati">Gabrio Casati</a> took power, while the democrat <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carlo-cattaneo">Carlo Cattaneo</a> led the council of war during the fighting.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The provisional government governed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lombardy">Lombardy</a> and called on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-albert-of-sardinia">Charles Albert</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-sardinia">Kingdom of Sardinia</a>, who declared war on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a>. Moderates led by Casati favoured union with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/piedmont">Piedmont</a>, while republicans such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carlo-cattaneo">Cattaneo</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/giuseppe-mazzini">Giuseppe Mazzini</a> wanted to delay the question. A plebiscite in May and June approved fusion with Piedmont.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After the Piedmontese defeat at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-custoza-1848">Custoza</a> in July 1848, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/joseph-radetzky-von-radetz">Radetzky</a> reoccupied <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/duchy-of-milan">Milan</a> on 6 August, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lombardy">Lombardy</a> returned to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-lombardy-venetia">Kingdom of Lombardy-Venetia</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/provisional-government-of-milan.jpg" alt="Provisional Government of Milan" width="320" height="240"><figcaption>Image: Carlo Bossoli · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Austriaci_in_ritirata_da_Milano_attraverso_Porta_Tosa,_data_alle_fiamme,_notte_del_22_marzo_1848_(di_Carlo_Bossoli).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1848 CE – 1848 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Milan</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Gabrio Casati, Carlo Cattaneo</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Italian, Lombard</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/italy">Italy</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Lombard Provisional Government (1848)</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1848&amp;focus=provisional-government-of-milan" aria-label="Provisional Government of Milan on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4898 574 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Provisional Government of Milan lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5218 830L5218 830M5218 830L5226 1028M5218 830L5381 747"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5218 830h0M5226 1028h0M5381 747h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5218 830h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5218 830h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1848&amp;focus=provisional-government-of-milan">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
